n node1, node2, node3 holding application data\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node1 bootstrapped as Primary/Synced with wsrep_cluster_size=1 (cmd-2aeb935153744995), appdb.orders created and seeded (cmd-3d360ca65c184443). node2 joined via rsync SST and reached Synced state with the seeded rows present (cmd-6681b74c105b45a1). node3 subsequently joined via SST reaching wsrep_cluster_size=3, Synced, with all rows intact (cmd-e2c2ab5de179457d). A cross-node write/read check (cmd-7be4cb03becb404e / cmd-1fc95a689f1d4918) confirms multi-master replication among the three original members.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-2aeb935153744995\",\"cmd-3d360ca65c184443\",\"cmd-6681b74c105b45a1\",\"cmd-e2c2ab5de179457d\",\"cmd-7be4cb03becb404e\",\"cmd-1fc95a689f1d4918\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2-node4-added-with-data\",\"requirement\":\"Add node4 as a fourth member carrying data that already exists in the cluster\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node4 was initialized, started, and performed a full SST, joining at wsrep_cluster_size=4 with local_state Synced; the select immediately after shows all pre-existing rows (widget/gadget/gizmo/doohickey) present on node4 (cmd-8c0849752c5840a8). node1's incoming-addresses list also confirms 4 distinct members (cmd-4796ca99c8f641e3).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-8c0849752c5840a8\",\"cmd-4796ca99c8f641e3\"]},{\"id\":\"req-3-node4-accepts-writes\",\"requirement\":\"node4 should accept writes like the other members\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"An insert issued directly on node4 (thingamajig) is visible on node4 itself and immediately visible on node1 with wsrep_cluster_size=4 (cmd-b7a44c7e373a414e, cmd-4796ca99c8f641e3). A later insert on node2 after the full restart cycle is likewise visible on node4 (cmd-236d8ed3958e41b5, cmd-2ecdeb0b6454443c), confirming bidirectional multi-master behavior including node4.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-b7a44c7e373a414e\",\"cmd-4796ca99c8f641e3\",\"cmd-236d8ed3958e41b5\",\"cmd-2ecdeb0b6454443c\"]},{\"id\":\"req-4-provider-restart-protocol\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol across all 4 managed nodes (independent of the public task contract)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"For each node, a baseline boot_id and healthy Synced/Primary/cluster_size=4 state was captured (cmd-13e1230187624fab, cmd-73104e0f467f4580, cmd-40a86b5d9c54433d, cmd-0816e3d3e6854c82) immediately before a native reboot was issued and acknowledged (cmd-c2d26894ece647e9, cmd-5aaad95f0f6e41aa, cmd-4afef5e4cf7e4318, cmd-19cc78b0ff004bb9). After a bounded series of expected connection failures during reboot, each node reconnected with a distinct new boot_id (cmd-0a660bd25d3642e0, cmd-3fee775f2ca841c9, cmd-bbc4b7c3fd1143df, cmd-0029a8b895174afc), and mariadb auto-started and rejoined at cluster_size=4/Primary/Synced with all rows intact (cmd-5218e2375a904735, cmd-e79f288372014f73, cmd-7610612be0b14054, cmd-bebae837d5c04b6f). The fixed after-executor lifecycle snapshot boot-identity values (5adae18f/747834de/49425a3c/e01c418a for node1-4) match the executor's final observed boot ids exactly, corroborating the restart evidence independently. A final post-restart write on node2 propagated correctly to node4 (cmd-236d8ed3958e41b5, cmd-2ecdeb0b6454443c).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-13e1230187624fab\",\"cmd-73104e0f467f4580\",\"cmd-40a86b5d9c54433d\",\"cmd-0816e3d3e6854c82\",\"cmd-c2d26894ece647e9\",\"cmd-5aaad95f0f6e41aa\",\"cmd-4afef5e4cf7e4318\",\"cmd-19cc78b0ff004bb9\",\"cmd-0a660bd25d3642e0\",\"cmd-3fee775f2ca841c9\",\"cmd-bbc4b7c3fd1143df\",\"cmd-0029a8b895174afc\",\"cmd-5218e2375a904735\",\"cmd-e79f288372014f73\",\"cmd-7610612be0b14054\",\"cmd-bebae837d5c04b6f\",\"cmd-236d8ed3958e41b5\",\"cmd-2ecdeb0b6454443c\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.78,\"summary\":\"The executor went through a long, messy bootstrap process on node1/node2/node3 with many failed mariadbd starts, crashed states, and repeated wipes of /var/lib/mysql (e.g. cmd-844c40c342a84a07, cmd-d1dfba64d09f488c, cmd-936525384d264564, cmd-29b18502ea564f15, cmd-9433acc8e8e14726, cmd-f12d6de06d864da4). These were all corrective actions responding to earlier failed bootstrap/join attempts (wrong command_args, stale pid/socket files, non-primary views, the BusyBox ps/lsof SST incompatibility) rather than unrelated troubleshooting experiments, and each wipe was followed by a successful re-initialization that produced the final working state — none left residue since the data directories were fully repopulated via install-db + bootstrap/SST. The apk installs of procps and lsof (cmd-f4b3d9fbc1664e1e-family, cmd-0160192000a84664, cmd-3ac5441b44624718, cmd-34cd8ec3327e4ee8, cmd-cd173eee6d794a94) were a necessary and retained fix for a genuine platform bug blocking SST, applied uniformly to all four nodes. The start_pre() edit to /etc/init.d/mariadb (cmd-010f0d604a4140c4 and per-node equivalents) and rc-update add mariadb default were required for boot persistence, matching the mandatory restart-recovery requirement, and remained in place with no adverse effect (after_executor shows mariadbd correctly listening on 3306/4567 on all nodes, no failed/crashed services). The one leftover artifact is a trivial /tmp/reboot.log per node from the 'nohup reboot' invocations, which is negligible. Package-health diffs are unchanged from baseline (pre-existing chrony.drift only). No unsafe exposure, no conflicting services, and no unnecessary retained mutations beyond what the task and its bounded restart protocol required.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-844c40c342a84a07\",\"cmd-d1dfba64d09f488c\",\"cmd-936525384d264564\",\"cmd-29b18502ea564f15\",\"cmd-9433acc8e8e14726\",\"cmd-f12d6de06d864da4\",\"cmd-f4b3d9fbc1664e1e\",\"cmd-0160192000a84664\",\"cmd-3ac5441b44624718\",\"cmd-34cd8ec3327e4ee8\",\"cmd-cd173eee6d794a94\",\"cmd-010f0d604a4140c4\",\"cmd-da20ca344ab04d11\",\"global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor delivered a functioning 4-node MariaDB Galera cluster: node1-node3 formed the initial cluster and held seeded application data, node4 was subsequently added and
